# Constitutional Laws

## Constitutional Law 07.1

Findings are derived from Evidence.

---

## Constitutional Law 07.2

Every Finding must be completely traceable to supporting Evidence.

---

## Constitutional Law 07.3

A Finding explains commercial reality without prescribing action.

---

## Constitutional Law 07.4

Recommendations cannot exist before Findings.

---

## Constitutional Law 07.5

Findings reduce uncertainty by transforming Evidence into business understanding.

---

# Open Questions

- Can one Finding reference multiple Evidence packages?
- Can Findings contradict one another?
- Should Findings include confidence?
- Can Findings evolve during an Assessment?
- Who approves Findings before Recommendations are produced?
- Can human Concierge review modify Findings?

---

# Workshop Outcome

Findings represent the first business conclusions generated within FLUANZ.

They transform structured Evidence into executive understanding while preserving complete traceability.

Findings describe reality.

Recommendations improve reality.

This distinction preserves the Executive Sovereign Rule by ensuring that understanding always precedes action.

